INT. CAR WASH - TUNNEL - NIGHT

Twenty-four hour. Neon blue. Brushes idle. Water drips.

SAL MORETTI (60s, bomber jacket, thick fingers) leans on a vacuum stand. Easy. Humming.

DANNY KAPLAN (30s, track jacket, nervous knee) sits on an upturned bucket. Eating sunflower seeds.

LEO PASQUALE (20s, hoodie, wire-thin) wipes a towel over a Cadillac. Slow. Careful.

SAL
Leo. You missed a spot.

LEO
Where?

SAL
Rear quarter. Left.

Leo wipes. Danny spits a shell.

DANNY
Sal, we doing this or what?

SAL
We're waiting.

DANNY
For what?

SAL
For the car to be clean, Danny. He's particular.

Danny laughs. Too loud. He stops.

DANNY
Who's particular?

SAL
The client. Come on. Eat your seeds.

Leo sets down the towel. Wipes his hands on his jeans. Glances at the Cadillac's trunk.

LEO
(softly)
How long's he been in there, Sal?

SAL
Who?

LEO
Don't. Please.

Sal's smile stays. His eyes don't.

SAL
Leo. I like you. You know that.

LEO
I know.

SAL
Your cousin Marcus told me about you. Said you were solid.

LEO
I am solid.

Danny stands. Slowly. The bucket rolls.

DANNY
Sal, what's he talking about?

SAL
Danny, sit down.

DANNY
Sal.

Sal pulls a revolver from his jacket. Not pointing it. Just holding.

SAL
Somebody in this tunnel's wearing a wire. He's been wearing it for three weeks.

Leo's hand drifts to his hoodie pocket. Stops.

DANNY
(to Leo)
Tell him it's not you.

LEO
It's not.

SAL
Danny. Open your jacket.

DANNY
What?

SAL
Open it. Slow.

Danny opens his track jacket. Under it, a small black box taped to his ribs. Thin red light blinking.

Silence. The brushes begin to turn.

DANNY
Sal. I can explain.

SAL
(gently)
I know you can.

He raises the gun.
